quran[9]{c,v,t}:
  28,51,"Indeed, We have caused the Word to reach them so that they may become mindful of advice."
  28,52,Those to whom We gave the Book before it—they are the ones who believe in it.
  28,53,"When it is recited to them, they say: ‘We believe in it. It is surely the truth from our Lord. Indeed, we were the ones who submitted (even) before it (came).’"
  28,54,These (believers) will be given their reward two times for having been patient. They repel evil with good and spend (in charity) from what We have provided them.
  28,55,"And when they hear vain talk, they turn away from it and say: ‘Our deeds belong to us, and your deeds belong to you. Peace be upon you! We do not seek (the company of) ignorant people.’"
  28,56,"You cannot guide whomever you wish, but Allah guides whomever He wills. And He knows best who are (rightly) guided."
  28,57,"They say: ‘If we follow the guidance with you, we shall be snatched away from our land.’ Have We not established a secure Sanctuary (i.e. Mecca) for them, where fruits of all kinds are brought as a provision from Us? But most of them do not know."
  28,58,How many a town have We destroyed who were spoiled by their (high standard of) living? So these are their (ruined) houses that were never inhabited after them except a few. And We are the (sole) Inheritors.
  28,59,And your Lord would never destroy the towns until He had raised a messenger in their mother city to recite to them Our Verses. And We would never destroy the towns except when their people were wrongdoers.
